#!/usr/bin/env sh
# #1574 gap (2) — locus-prefix pre-commit backstop. The #883 stack guards the Edit/Write tools (the
# PreToolUse `--pre` hook) and the backlog.mjs CLI write path (#1574 gap 1), but a `cat >>` / heredoc
# body-append still reaches disk unguarded. This hook runs the SAME staged sweep on every commit, so a
# bare code-path ref in a staged backlog/*.md or reports/*.md is caught here — regardless of HOW it landed —
# rather than at check:standards close-out. `lint:locus` (= lint-locus-prefix.mjs --staged) exits 2 on a
# finding, which blocks the commit. Wired via `core.hooksPath .githooks` (set by the `prepare` npm script).
#
# IMPORTANT: each gate must fail-fast to preserve its own exit code — in sh, the script exits with the
# last command's exit code, so sequencing without fail-fast silently swallows earlier failures. Use
# `|| exit $?` after each gate so the first failure stops the hook and propagates the right exit code.

# Placeholder git author guard (2026-10-05..20 incident: every lane commit was authored "test"). Lane clones
# only; refuses only a placeholder/missing author or committer — a real identity always passes.
node scripts/guard-git-identity.mjs || exit $?

npm run --silent lint:locus || exit $?

# Inventory write-time regen (#3071-adjacent incident, PR #1404 — a research topic was added without
# `gen:inventory`, and the stale AGENTS.md count wasn't caught until CI failed on an already-
# `review:accepted` PR, costing a full round-trip). `gen:inventory --staged` is a self-contained AUTO-FIX,
# not a blocking gate: it no-ops unless the commit stages an inventory-affecting file (a per-entry
# registry under src/_data/{blocks,plugs,intents,semantics,researchTopics,projects}/ or AGENTS.md
# itself), and when it regenerates it writes the new AGENTS.md blob directly into the INDEX (git
# update-index — never a working-tree `git add`, which would risk sweeping an unrelated unstaged
# AGENTS.md edit into the commit, #1414 review) — so a normal `git commit` that touches
# inventory-affecting content simply can't produce a stale AGENTS.md. Counts are read from the git
# INDEX too (not readdirSync over the working tree, #1414 review round 2), so an untracked sibling
# file dropped in a registry dir can't inflate the committed count either. Costs under a fraction of
# a second (measured) since it only reads the small per-entry JSON registries, so it runs
# unconditionally rather than trying to be cleverer about scoping. `check:standards`'s `kind: 'inventory'`
# check stays as a CI backstop for any commit path that bypasses this hook (e.g. `--no-verify`).
npm run --silent gen:inventory:staged || exit $?

# #2179's pre-commit verdict/mtime gate (scripts/check-visual-baseline-update.mjs) is RETIRED (#2238):
# it deadlocked the CI baseline-refresh workflow, which can never author a verdict that postdates its
# own regenerated PNG. Baseline review now happens in the PR that carries the changed snapshot(s) — the
# rendered image diff IS the review surface (see .github/workflows/update-visual-baselines.yml and
# #2183's blanket "changes land via reviewed PR" rule) — so no separate sidecar gate is needed here.
